target = 7
print(find_pairs(numbers, target))
```

This program first creates a dictionary to store the counts of each number in the list. Then, it iterates through the dictionary to find all unique pairs that add up to the target sum. The order of the pairs in the output does not matter, so the list is sorted before returning.
